=== MANUAL FIX 1: Eventf format string issues ===
Classification: SYSTEMATIC
Pattern name: printf-format-string-vet
Description: k8s 1.36 (Go 1.26) enforces stricter go vet printf checking on Eventf/Warningf calls.
  Two sub-patterns found:
  (a) Format-arg mismatch: Eventf has more args than format verbs (fix: add missing %s/%v verb)
  (b) Non-constant format string: variable passed as format arg (fix: wrap with "%s", var)
Detection command: go vet ./... 2>&1 | grep -E 'printf|Sprintf|Eventf|format'
  Alternative: grep -rn '\.Eventf(' --include='*.go' | grep -v vendor/ | grep -v '%'
Fix command: For (b) non-constant format strings, automatable with sed:
  grep -rn '\.Eventf(.*EventType\w\+, "[^"]*", [a-z]' --include='*.go' | grep -v vendor/
  Then wrap the variable arg: sed 's/Eventf(\(.*\), \(errMsg\|msg\))/Eventf(\1, "%s", \2)/'
  For (a) mismatched verbs, requires AST analysis or manual review of go vet output.
Scope: GENERIC - affects any Go project using client-go EventRecorder with Go >=1.26
Files changed: cmd/cert-approver/main.go, pkg/k8sclient/k8sclient.go (2 files, 2 lines)

